Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:32:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Improve filename identification with progressive fallback
 searches

Add GetSearchAttempts method to TmdbUtils that generates progressively less
specific search attempts: full name+year, name without year, then
progressively shorter names (dropping trailing words) that often contain
release tags. This helps when filenames have non-standard tags that survive
initial cleaning.

Applied to both movie and series TMDb providers (GetSearchResults and
GetMetadata) so failed searches automatically retry with simplified names
before giving up. Also expanded CleanStrings regex with modern release tags
(av1, hevc, remux, 10bit, hdr10, atmos, criterion, dsnp, etc.) to improve
automatic noise removal during filename parsing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
